ref_completion:
Let the roots of $x^3 + Px^2 + Qx - 19 = 0$ be $r_1, r_2, r_3$.
Let the roots of $x^3 - Ax^2 + Bx - C = 0$ be $s_1, s_2, s_3$.
We are given that $r_i = s_i + 1$ for $i = 1, 2, 3$.
By Vieta's formulas, we have
\begin{align*} r_1 + r_2 + r_3 &= -P \\ r_1 r_2 + r_1 r_3 + r_2 r_3 &= Q \\ r_1 r_2 r_3 &= 19 \end{align*}
and
\begin{align*} s_1 + s_2 + s_3 &= A \\ s_1 s_2 + s_1 s_3 + s_2 s_3 &= B \\ s_1 s_2 s_3 &= C \end{align*}
Since $r_i = s_i + 1$, we have
\begin{align*} r_1 + r_2 + r_3 &= (s_1 + 1) + (s_2 + 1) + (s_3 + 1) = s_1 + s_2 + s_3 + 3 = A + 3 \\ r_1 r_2 + r_1 r_3 + r_2 r_3 &= (s_1 + 1)(s_2 + 1) + (s_1 + 1)(s_3 + 1) + (s_2 + 1)(s_3 + 1) \\ &= (s_1 s_2 + s_1 + s_2 + 1) + (s_1 s_3 + s_1 + s_3 + 1) + (s_2 s_3 + s_2 + s_3 + 1) \\ &= (s_1 s_2 + s_1 s_3 + s_2 s_3) + 2(s_1 + s_2 + s_3) + 3 = B + 2A + 3 \\ r_1 r_2 r_3 &= (s_1 + 1)(s_2 + 1)(s_3 + 1) = (s_1 + 1)(s_2 s_3 + s_2 + s_3 + 1) \\ &= s_1 s_2 s_3 + s_1 s_2 + s_1 s_3 + s_1 + s_2 s_3 + s_2 + s_3 + 1 \\ &= s_1 s_2 s_3 + (s_1 s_2 + s_1 s_3 + s_2 s_3) + (s_1 + s_2 + s_3) + 1 = C + B + A + 1 \end{align*}
We have
\begin{align*} -P &= A + 3 \\ Q &= B + 2A + 3 \\ 19 &= C + B + A + 1 \end{align*}
Thus, $A + B + C = 19 - 1 - A = 18 - A$.
We want to find $A + B + C$.
From the equations above, we have
\begin{align*} P &= -A - 3 \\ Q &= B + 2A + 3 \\ C &= 18 - A - B \end{align*}
Then
\begin{align*} A + B + C &= A + B + (18 - A - B) = 18 \end{align*}

Final Answer: The final answer is $\boxed{18}$

