Since the plane contains the vector $\begin{pmatrix} 1 \\ 2 \\ 3 \end{pmatrix}$, we can take $\mathbf{p} = \begin{pmatrix} 1 \\ 2 \\ 3 \end{pmatrix}$. Then the equation of the plane is
\begin{align*} \begin{pmatrix} 4 \\ 5 \\ 6 \end{pmatrix} \cdot \begin{pmatrix} x - 1 \\ y - 2 \\ z - 3 \end{pmatrix} &= 0 \\ 4(x - 1) + 5(y - 2) + 6(z - 3) &= 0 \\ 4x - 4 + 5y - 10 + 6z - 18 &= 0 \\ 4x + 5y + 6z &= 32 \end{align*}
